rota lap 4469, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; its threshold says the concrete fact outranks the plausible story, and this lap spent itself on two facts read at the door rather than reasoned about
think The cold open refused: another roster pass held the lock. Read its owner rather than assuming a peer -- /proc/4130089/cwd named this tree, and the runner's own refusal printed parent=gone group_leader=gone lap=gone. An orphan.
think Proved it void before touching it. Its transcript recorded stashed_entries=20 with stash@{0} at 20260909-092434; git stash list here reads 21 with 20260909-192107 on top, so my own round-open moved the tree it had digested. Its verdict was fixed at tree_moved and it held the lock for another half hour. The runner's comment names exactly this and says a hand acts.
think Signalled through tools/f/fleet_call.sh, which resolved seventeen candidates and refused twelve peer trees by name. One in this tree, TERM, lock released by its own trap.
think Read what the round-open had stashed and found a whole lap: 218 insertions, a new control, a witness leg, two REDS shelves, a card account and its own session log, status GREEN with a hot pass already run, cut at its send two minutes before my open.
think Re-proved it rather than trusting its status line: glow_rune_alphabet GREEN, standing_equipment_redleg GREEN at 53 of 53, and the five ledger guards green. Landed and pushed to both remotes before opening my own work, so the same cut cannot take it twice.
think That lap's own recommend was my handoff, and it had already corrected my elder card line: the census grep covers convergence_(tree_)?prove.sh, so the gap was subjects rather than spelling -- exactly one tool had ever been handed to the tree prover.
obs readme_metrics_splice.sh is a third shape beside the flag and the single path: it takes two paths, the target and the block. convergence_prove.sh invokes sh <tool> <one-path>, so it hands the splice one argument and reads verdict=refused at the splice's own ${2:?}. Measured, not argued. The tree prover's argument list is variadic and reached it with no change to the instrument at all.
obs The perturbation is anchored on the begin marker rather than on a row of the block, because the rows are generated metrics free to change and the marker is the one thing the splice's contract requires. A sample that stopped landing would read perturb_inert rather than blaming the tool.
obs proven_by_prover_run measures whether somebody ASKED, which is a different fact from whether a tool converges. It read 1 for a day with the instrument rostered and running every lap.
obs The card stood at 40,958 of 40,960, so the new account had to fit the elder's weight to the byte; five passes of trimming brought it from 1,515 to under 878.
